node_modules/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
docs/.vitepress/cache/
*.local
.DS_Store
.caliber/
# Agent config is machine-local EXCEPT the authoring rules, which are repo
# knowledge and are tracked. This must be written as an exclusion of the
# directory's CONTENTS (`.claude/*`) plus a re-inclusion of the `rules/`
# directory itself. A plain `.claude/` exclusion would make git skip the
# directory entirely and never evaluate any `!` negation inside it, so
# `.claude/` + `!.claude/rules/*.md` silently tracks nothing.
.claude/*
!.claude/rules/
CALIBER_LEARNINGS.md
docs/old/
coverage/
